  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 247 PM EDT Mon Sep 21 2026\n\nWednesday - Monday...\n\nThe overall upper pattern will be pretty interesting by mid week as \nit will feature hybrid Omega/Rex blocking near and over our region. \nThe main part of the Omega Block will stretch from the western Gulf \nCoast states up into eastern Canada. Meanwhile, the Rex Block will \ntake shape as a cutoff low settles over Ohio. This closed upper low \nwill be close enough to our region to support a few lingering precip \nchances mainly along the I-75 corridor on Wednesday. Outside of \nthat, the rest of the CWA should be dry. Temperatures will be \nseasonable for this time of year ranging from the low 70s across \nsouthern IN to the upper 70s across southern KY.\n\nAs we move through late week, the aforementioned closed upper low \nwill center more over the mid Atlantic states, with the Omega block \ngetting a bit more established over our area. This will keep us dry, \nlikely lasting through the weekend, possibly into early next week. \nTemperatures will continue to be seasonal for this time of year with \nhighs in the 70s heading into the weekend. By Sunday/Monday, temps \nwill likely start to trend back above normal and more into the low \n80s. It's also worth noting that some cool/crisp mornings will be in \nstore, with Saturday/Sunday mornings being the coolest. Looking for \nlows in the upper 40s and low 50s.",
